# p5 mcp config: fx v0.0.16 notes a key it reads and no longer acts on
# (`noteIgnoredKeys`): `required`, and a `restart_limit` other than 1. xfx
# acts on both and gives no such note (docs/parity.md, the profile row).
fx: homefile .fx/mcp.json p5-mcp-config-ignored-profile.json
xfx: homefile .xfx/mcp.json p5-mcp-config-ignored-profile.json
keep
wait 12
# The status line keeps its MCP text back while a server is still
# starting, up to 10 s (statusline.rs MCP_STARTUP_QUIET,
# menu.zig:443@481104fd). The snap is the config's problems once fx says
# them, not a second count 2 s past the 10 (FLAKE-HINT4). xfx says nothing
# of them -- a difference, not a timing -- so only fx waits.
fx: until shown MCP config has 2 problems
snap startup
type /mcp
key Enter
wait 2
snap menu
key Escape
wait 0.5
key C-u
type /mcp list
key Enter
wait 2
snap list
key Escape
wait 0.3
key C-u
snapfull end
